 In frame 22, the adult has an expressive, possibly excited or surprised face, but this is in reaction to the reindeer, not the snowmobile. There are no gestures or actions indicating frustration, repair attempts, or mechanical troubleshooting.\n\n---\n\n### Temporal Sequence Context:\n\n- **Frames 1–8:** Show aftermath of hunting — bloody hands, bag of entrails being placed in snowmobile storage. This confirms the “second hunting” context.\n- **Frames 9–16:** Transition to snowmobile travel — moving along a snowy road, encountering a reindeer.\n- **Frames 17–26:** Snowmobile is stopped; people observe and interact with the reindeer.\n- **Frames 27–30:** Snowmobile is parked near buildings and a snowplow — people are observing their surroundings, not dealing with vehicle issues.\n\nThere is **no point** in the sequence where the snowmobile is shown to have a reverse gear problem or any mechanical issue preventing movement.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion:\n\nThe claim that “their snowmobile can’t reverse” is **not supported** by any visual evidence in the provided frames. The snowmobile is functional, used for transportation, and only stationary when intentionally stopped for observation or interaction. The family members show no signs of distress or mechanical troubleshooting.\n\n✅ **Answer ‘4’ is incorrect.**"}, {'batch_start': 330, 'batch_end': 360, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1765.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1766.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1767.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1768.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1769.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1770.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1771.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1772.jpg', '/mnt/ss